idance.\n\n**Rule 6c-11:** Sets conditions for index-based and transparent-portfolio ETFs to operate without individual exemptive orders, including custom-basket policies and daily portfolio disclosure. It doesn't prescribe a specific authorized participant (AP) agreement form or detail permitted AP counterparties; confirm this in the rule text.\n\n**Clearing/settlement:** In-kind creations and redemptions generally run through NSCC/DTC. APs are typically registered broker-dealers and DTC participants, and fund shares must be DTC-eligible.\n\n**Distinguishing parties:** The rule's counterparties are APs, broker-dealers acting under fund arrangements. The bank's forms may add parties (transfer agent, custodian, distributor) and contractual requirements beyond the rule.","ttft_ms":8276,"type":"result","duration_ms":9263,"uuid":"301f271c-4df1-4e21-87ea-b2097c3dcbad","ttft_stream_ms":425,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":425,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
